    "step_results": [
      "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n1. **Missing named export in `src/finetune/index.js`**: The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export. Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`.\n\n2. **Incorrect function signature in `src/eval/metrics.js`**: The `toxicityMetric` function had a signature `(outputs, bannedTerms)` that was inconsistent with other metrics. When `runEvaluations` called it with `(outputs, references)`, the references array was being passed as `bannedTerms`, causing the function to treat reference text as toxic keywords. Fixed by changing the signature to `(outputs, references)` and hardcoding the use of `defaultBannedTerms`.\n\n**Test results**: All 28 tests passing \u2713"
